 "notes": "Printed: '... X is the number of creatures that died under YOUR CONTROL this turn.' The opponent steals your 1/1 with Enthralling Hold; on their later turn it attacks you for them (attackers + your life 19 prove they control it) and dies under THEIR control (into YOUR graveyard, its owner's). Your Bearer is then put onto the battlefield that turn: no creature died under your control, X = 0. Hand: Bearer + your turn-3 draw (Library 5) - Bearer = 1; library Library 4..0. A count by graveyard owner draws 1 here (stronger than printed). (V2: the opponent's mana is added on its own turn, where it casts the Hold.)"
